Z||000001||mrfixit58||04-09-2001||04:19 PM||||I'm going to take a wild shot at this and say, "You've never heard of BubbaJoexx or seen his web site, have you?".<P>BubbaJoexx is the current king of the 4.9 swaps. He just posted on his web site, a carbed 4.9 with a 4:10 4-speed tranny that he says will get the front end off the ground.<P>Visit him here: <A HREF="http://sites.netscape.net/bubbajoexx/homepage" TARGET=_blank>http://sites.netscape.net/bubbajoexx/homepage</A> <P>You can also do a search on "4.9" and get a lot of info.<P>Have fun,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||6
Z||000002||rockcrawl||04-09-2001||06:51 PM||||Don't do it man! Leave the port injection on there. Detroit hasn't made a carbuerated auto since the mid eighties, for many good reasons. But if you must do it, get an intake and valve covers from a TBI 4.1 or 4.5 and make a simple adapter.<P>Here are some pics of my 4.5 PFI engine almost ready to go. I will be keeping the fuel injection.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/45PFI1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/45PFI3.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||04-10-2001||08:30 AM||||Rockcrawl,<P>That motor looks great! I've really been stewing over this motor conversion for some time now. I've got the bug and I've got it bad! I may be sending you an e-mail for some "user" insite in the near future.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||LAMBO||04-10-2001||02:15 PM||||This site may have what you are looking for. <A HREF="http://www.chrfab.com/index.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.chrfab.com/index.htm</A> <BR>Hope this helps.<BR>Todd||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||04-10-2001||04:05 PM||||chrfab.com does northstar mods, the 4.9 is not a Northstar. <P>I've decided that my Testarossa project is going to take way too long to finish, so I pushed it aside and I'm slowly collecting parts for it, including a 4.9 and Getrag. Meanwhile I'm still addicted to Fieros and I just can't wait to build up another one. So I located the 180/275 4.5 PFI and an '85 GT. I hope to have the two mated in time for the Carlisle show.<BR>Just to give you an idea of how inexpensive these engines are, I paid $350 for a '91 Deville 4.9 that runs and drives, and $50 for the 4.5 engine from a '90 Deville including wiring and ECM. My '87 4.1 Deville donor was given to me free. Add that to the fact that they weigh only as much as a 2.8, and you see how great this swap really is.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfixit58||04-10-2001||04:14 PM||||ROCK!!! Free! $50! $350! Your killing me, man!<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
